item~ function src/phext.rs :: get_subspace_coordinates :: pub fn get_subspace_coordinates(subspace: &[u8], target: Coordinate) -> (usize, usize, Coordinate) { :: finds the start and end offsets for the given coordinate Returns `(start, end, best)`: when the document reaches `target`, `start..end` is that scroll's text (empty if it has none) and `best` is `target`; otherwise `start == end` is where the scroll would go: just before the break that steps past `target`, or the end of the document. `best` is the coordinate in effect there, so writing breaks from `best` up to `target` and then the text places it correctly. The walker only moves on a dimension break, so it is compared with `target` only at the start and after each break, and the scan stops as soon as it steps past `target`. Earlier versions returned `start = 0` for a missing coordinate that falls between two scrolls, so `fetch`, `replace`, and `remove` acted on the scroll before it, and they missed a scroll reached only by breaks at the very end of the document. :: direct :: api
item~ function src/phext.rs :: offset :: pub fn offset(phext: &str, coord: Coordinate) -> usize { :: The offset of the scroll at `coord`, or of the last scroll before it. 0 when no scroll comes at or before `coord` (earlier versions panicked there). :: direct :: api
