item~ struct src/phext.rs :: Coordinate :: pub struct Coordinate { :: provides access to a default-initialized coordinate at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1 phext coordinates are formed along a 9-dimensional hierarchy with three main arms of the form z3.z2.z1/y3.y2.y1.x3.x2.x1 where: Z - this arm contains the library (z3), shelf (z2), and series (z1) dimensions Y - this arm contains the collection (y3), volume (y2), and book (y1) dimensions X - this arm contains the chapter (x3), section (x2), and scroll (x1) dimensions Dense graphs: phext is sparse by design. Coordinate components are unbounded, but a fully-populated dense graph contains the product of its dimensions' extents in scrolls — a dense block spanning 1000 in each of 9 dimensions implies 10^27 scrolls. Materializing, exploding, or indexing such a graph costs memory proportional to its populated scroll count. The old 999 cap never protected against this (999^9 was already unreachable); sparsity does. Keep graphs sparse. :: direct :: api
item- const src/phext.rs :: COORDINATE_MAXIMUM
