item~ function src/phext.rs :: verify_commit :: pub fn verify_commit(input: &str, entries: &[Coordinate], commit: Coordinate) -> bool { :: true when the scroll at `commit` is a commit marker whose count matches `entries` and whose checksum matches the entries' current contents, in order. Any missing, altered, or torn entry — or a missing marker — yields false: the batch did not commit. The document is indexed with a single `explode` pass and the marker and every entry are read from that map. The previous implementation ran the scanning `fetch` once for the marker and once per entry, so verification cost grew quadratically in document length — the cost a WAL recovery pass pays over the whole log, per transaction. :: direct :: api
